1.0
  Initial release
1.0rc2
  Cleaned up code
10.rc3
  changed char fields to unsigned char
  Changed many functions to return status
  Added macros for __FUNCTION__ keyword, for compiler sanity
  Added include headers needed for other UNIX platforms
1.0rc4
  Changed cfg->connection to cfg->conn_type
  Added support for send file text to connections on actions
  If data received while off-hook and no conn, go on-hook.
  Clean up parseRegister action in getcmd.c
  Add support for ':' and '-' extended commands
  Cleaned up functions to only exit at one point
1.0rc5
  Moved includes to be in correct order
  Fixed Q0 and Q1 (they were reversed)
1.0rc6
  Add support for direct connection
1.0rc7
  Fixed mislocated tcsetattr in serial.com:ser_init_conn
1.0rc8
  Fixed bug in ip_thread (calling a null number would turn on ip_thread, but no connection, generating a dump
  Fixed bugs in dce_set_flow_control
  Fixed behavior of parms parsing for &Z (complex) and S (simple)
  Defaulted code to not assume /dev/ttyS0 as serport
1.0rc9
  Fixed bug that would stop first session if second call came in
  Fixed outbound call not bringing DCD high.
1.0rc10
  Added some more debugging information
  Changed logging to go to stdout from stderr
  Fixed Phone book matching function to use logger
1.0rc11
  Added ip232 support with custom protocol for use with matching modified version of WinVICE 1.19
  Added full support for Telnet Binary Transmission (RFC 856)
1.0rc12
  Added code to hook SIG_IO to SIG_IGN.  Newer versions of Linux are terminating when IO arrives.
1.1rc1
  Rationalized data types for binary versus textual data
  Merged in Gene Buckle's change to allow binding to a specific IP address
  Merged in (or re-implemented) Chris Osborn changes (https://github.com/FozzTexx/tcpser) 
    Strip parity when looking for commands, generate matching parity on modem responses
    Fixed bug in sending telnet sub-options. Now tcpser can connect to real telnet servers.  
  Added in support for raw rs232 data tracing, while retaining serial port tracing
  Cleaned up lots of bad decisions around variable names, where functions should live, etc.1.2.0 (ELiTE RETRO BBS EDiTiON — fork by David Jacoby)
  Pre-connect bot gate: BACKSPACE x2 (-x) or password (-k), with timeout (-W)
  Persistent IP blocklist + allowlist, per-IP rate limiting, gate-fail auto-block (-F)
  Live full-screen terminal dashboard (-M) with hotkeys
  Web dashboard over HTTP (-H), connection CSV log (-O), stats persistence (-Y)
  Event webhooks (-e), external gate-success hook (-E, sandboxed)
  BBS recovery watchdog (-w), max session time (-m), USB-serial auto-reconnect
  RS232 adapter analyzer/diagnostic mode (-Z)
  PETSCII pre-connect banner/access screens (-P/-G), telnet NVT negotiation
1.2.1 (security/stability audit round)
  SECURITY: fixed serial AT-parser out-of-bounds write (backspace underflow, ATE0)
  SECURITY: capped + throttled password-gate guesses per connection (brute force)
  SECURITY: fixed global accept() freeze DoS (one silent caller blocked all ports)
  SECURITY: web dashboard now defaults to 127.0.0.1, optional token auth, I/O
            timeouts, bounded handler-thread pool
  SECURITY: constant-time password/token compare; webhook URL kept out of ps;
            connection log created mode 0600; blocklist no longer wiped on
            missing file; full blocklist table evicts oldest instead of allowing
  Hardening: stack protector, FORTIFY_SOURCE, format-security, PIE/RELRO
  Robustness: NULL-guarded localtime, fixed spawn_thread return check, ctype UB
              casts, sig_atomic_t signal flags, select-error fall-through fix
  Features: Prometheus /metrics endpoint, multiple webhook targets + security
            events, graceful shutdown drain
  Quality: removed dead code, consolidated shared helpers into util.c, redesigned
           --help, added LICENSE + docs index, fixed inaccurate docs and man page
1.2.2 (security follow-up)
  SECURITY: -k env:VAR reads the gate password from an environment variable so
            it is no longer exposed in the process table (ps)
  SECURITY: statistics file (-Y) created mode 0600 (it persists caller IPs)
  SECURITY: webhook child resets PATH before exec so an inherited/hijacked PATH
            cannot substitute a malicious curl
1.2.3 (final audit cleanup — no findings left open)
  SECURITY: secure_script rejects symlinks (lstat) and execs via O_NOFOLLOW +
            fexecve (Linux) / execv, closing the validate->exec TOCTOU window
  SECURITY: web dashboard reader threads take the dashboard mutex for a
            consistent g_dash snapshot (data race closed); serial_fd/modem_cfg
            set through locked setters
  CLEANUP:  removed unused get_safe_config_path() (env paths still validated by
            validate_file_path: canonicalized + traversal-checked)
